{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01SMVv1yAkhdxn245jCp7Sji","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t# metadata-forensics — technique log (days 1-9; updated after every day)\n2\t\n3\tHow this lane has looked so far (observations, not guarantees):\n4\t- **Timed variants MUTATE** (organizer, Day 8: \"new, dynamic variations/mutations ... new unseen effects\"): nothing below is a\n5\t  guarantee for Time Trial / Mastery -- solvers derive structure and degrade per field.\n6\t- Every day = ONE evidence zip (`metadata-day-NN-evidence.zip`, plain Deflate, no password so far). Days 1-7: one tiny\n7\t  member (33 B - 3 KB) and ONE structural fact. Day 8+: the zip carries the whole cumulative kit (note + jpg + png + pdf +\n8\t  inner zip [+ D9 a 1.26 MB PE `.exe`]) and even the SINGLE contract asks every field (D8 12, D9 13 = identity + every\n9\t  earlier day's field + the new one). The member can itself be a container (D7/8: an inner ZIP whose own EOCD / CD is\n10\t  the asked field). Each day adds ONE member + ONE field; the previous kit members are byte-identical except the case id.\n11\t- Day 9 crossed into EXECUTABLE headers (`pe.coff_machine_u16_hex`): the metadata lane now parses binaries too, but only\n12\t  the raw header field -- answer the u16 as hex, not the binary lane's machine word (`i386`).\n13\t- A new `<fmt>.<field>` family each day: identity (name/size/hashes) -> magic prefix -> `text.utf8_bom_present` ->\n14\t  `jpeg.sof_dimensions_pixels` -> `png.ihdr_dimensions_pixels` -> `pdf.header_version` -> `zip.eocd_total_entries` ->\n15\t  `zip.central_directory_member_names` -> `pe.coff_machine_u16_hex`. Since Day 3 the question literally names the field\n16\t  (`Determine <fmt>.<field> for <member>`); answer ids read `dNN-<fmt>-NNN-<fmt>-<field>` (`.`/`_` -> `-`). NOTE the\n17\t  `dNN` is the drop/member family, not the day the field appeared: Day 8's new field came as `d07-zip-001-zip-central-\n18\t  directory-member-names`; Day 9's as `d09-pe-001-pe-coff-machine-u16-hex` (new member family -> new `dNN`).\n19\t- The prompt's flavor text describes decoys (impostors, renamed copies, \"-with-bom\" names, EXIF/presentation lies, chunk\n20\t  \"passengers\", catalog /Version overrides, \"impossible provenance\" names). The asked field so far was always the\n21\t  STRUCTURAL truth from the header/record bytes; names/extensions/secondary metadata are the lie. All 9 single solves were\n22\t  first-submit CORRECT in ~27-60 s; every TT/Mastery since Homebase (D4+) CORRECT first try.\n23\t- The flavor promises MORE than the sample delivers (D9: \"executables for several architectures, plus decoys wearing\n24\t  executable extensions\" -> one honest i386 PE, no ELF/Mach-O/decoy in any mode). Expect the promised cases to arrive\n25\t  later as mutations; pre-arm the sibling parsers (ELF/Mach-O/decoy -> `none`) without guessing their spellings.\n26\t- Titles are puns, not format hints: Day 7 \"Seven-Zip, No Relation\" was plain ZIP (PKWARE), no .7z anywhere.\n27\t\n28\t## Variant axes (what differs between the single, Time Trial and Mastery variants -- parse every value listed)\n29\t- **Delivery layout** -- see \"Delivery layouts seen\" below; resolve the named member through whatever wrapper arrives.\n30\t- **Decoys** -- renamed copies, misleading extensions/names, secondary metadata (EXIF, catalog /Version) that disagree\n31\t  with the header: always answer from the structural header bytes of the member the question names.\n32\t- **Member and values** -- names, sizes, dimensions and counts re-roll per variant; nothing about the sample is\n33\t  constant (Day 7 entry count went 2/3/4/5 with drop number 001-004; member names `room-NN/item-K.txt`). Day 8 re-rolled\n34\t  ONLY the note's case id (`Case <hex> evidence note.`, 33 B) -> md5/sha1/sha256/magic differ per set; jpg 257x146, png\n35\t  269x153, pdf 1.4, eocd 2, CD names identical across single/TT/5 Mastery sets. D9 same, plus the PE: Machine 0x014c in\n36\t  all 7 copies but the exe's sha256 differs per set (re-built per variant). Never cache a value across sets anyway.\n37\t- **ESCALATED field set** -- the contract grows over time: D7 TT/Mastery went 1 -> 11 fields (Mastery 22); D8 started at\n38\t  12 already in single (TT 12, Mastery 5 sets x 12 = 60); D9 13 (TT 13, Mastery 5 x 13 = 65). Families: the day's field +\n39\t  `evidence-note-{filename,size-bytes,md5,sha1,sha256,magic-prefix-hex-16,text-utf8-bom-present}` + carry-overs\n40\t  `d04-jpeg-*-sof-dimensions-pixels`, `d05-png-*-ihdr-dimensions-pixels`, `d06-pdf-*-header-version`, `d07-zip-*-eocd-\n41\t  total-entries`, `d07-zip-*-central-directory-member-names`, `d09-pe-*-pe-coff-machine-u16-hex`. Dispatch on the\n42\t  answer-id SUFFIX and keep EVERY earlier family answerable (reference: `challenges/day09/metadata-built-different/\n43\t  solver/solve.py` answers all 13 + a pre-armed `elf-e-machine-u16-hex` branch).\n44\t- **Answer kinds** -- `exact_text`, `integer`, `pattern` (hashes, case-insensitive; D9 also `0x`-hex with `trim` only,\n45\t  so case MATTERS -> lowercase), `enum` (`accepted_values`), and since D8 `json` (\"compact valid JSON array with exact\n46\t  values and order\"). Emit per `answer_format.kind`; read `syntax` for prefix/case (`0x` yes for u16_hex, no for magic).\n47\t- **Question-text tags** (D9 TT/Mastery, new): the first question gets ` [assigned-artifact-sha256:<64 hex>]` appended\n48\t  (Mastery: the bundle's sha, same for every set). Strip `\\s*\\[[^\\]]*\\]$` before reading a member name from question\n49\t  text; route by `answer_id` + `artifact` instead (the D9 solver was unaffected for that reason).\n50\t- **Nesting depth** -- the asked file may sit 2-3 zips deep (Mastery D7: outer -> `...-evidence-0N.zip` ->\n51\t  `evidence-drop-00N.zip`); resolve by the name after `->`, never answer from an enclosing zip.\n52\t\n53\t## Recognition cues -> first move\n54\t| You see | First move |\n55\t|---|---|\n56\t| `<zip> -> <member>` in `questions[].artifact` | `7z l -slt <zip>` then `7z x -o work/ <zip>`; (or python `zipfile` read of the member) |\n57\t| filename / size / md5 / sha1 / sha256 | `stat -c %s`, `md5sum sha1sum sha256sum` on the extracted member (bytes, not the zip entry name) |\n58\t| \"first sixteen bytes\", \"magic\", \"extension claims\" | `xxd -p -l 16 <member>` (lowercase, no spaces); `file -k` only for orientation |\n59\t| `text.*_bom_present` | `xxd -l 4`: UTF-8 BOM = `ef bb bf` (UTF-16LE `ff fe`, BE `fe ff`, UTF-32LE `ff fe 00 00`) -> `true`/`false` |\n60\t| `jpeg.*dimensions*` / SOF | walk JPEG segments from `ffd8` by length to SOFn (`ffc0..ffcf` minus c4/c8/cc): P, Y=height, X=width. `exiftool -ImageSize` cross-check only |\n61\t| `png.ihdr_*` / \"walk their chunks\" | `xxd -s 16 -l 8` = IHDR width,height (BE u32). Chunk walk = len/type/data/CRC loop (`lib.stego.png_chunks`) |\n62\t| `zip.eocd_*` / \"count what the archives claim\" | of the NAMED inner zip (not the evidence zip): last `PK\\x05\\x06` whose comment len reaches EOF; u16 @+8 disk entries, @+10 total, u32 @+12 cd size, @+16 cd offset, u16 @+20 comment len. `0xFFFF` -> ZIP64 locator `PK\\x06\\x07` (EOCD-20) -> `PK\\x06\\x06` u64 @+32. Cross-check: count `PK\\x01\\x02` walking from cd offset, `PK\\x03\\x04` |\n63\t| `zip.central_directory_*` / \"inventory every stored path, preserve directory context\" | walk `PK\\x01\\x02` from EOCD cd-offset (fallback `EOCD - cd_size` if data prepended): name len u16 @+28, extra @+30, comment @+32, name at +46; next = +46+n+e+c. Raw stored path, CD order, no basename/dedupe/sort; decode UTF-8 (flag bit 11 `0x800`, else try UTF-8 then cp437). `7z l -slt` / `zipinfo -1` as cross-check |\n64\t| `pdf.header_version` / \"declared versions\" | `head -c 16 <f> | xxd` -> `%PDF-x.y` at offset 0; `grep -a -o '/Version[^/>]*'` only as a diagnostic |\n65\t| `pe.coff_*` / \"executables for several architectures\", `.exe`/`.dll`/`.sys` | `MZ`@0 -> e_lfanew u32 LE @0x3C -> require `PE\\0\\0` there -> COFF FileHeader: Machine u16 @+4, NumberOfSections @+6, TimeDateStamp @+8, SizeOfOptionalHeader @+20, Characteristics @+22; OptionalHeader magic @+24 (`0x10b` PE32 / `0x20b` PE32+). `xxd -s $((0x3c)) -l 4` then `xxd -s <lfanew> -l 8`. `file`/`pefile` cross-check only |\n66\t| `elf.*` / `macho.*` siblings (promised \"several architectures\", not yet asked) | ELF: `\\x7fELF`, EI_DATA @5 picks endianness, e_machine u16 @18. Mach-O: `feedface`/`feedfacf` (either byte order) cputype u32 @4; fat `cafebabe` = BE nfat_arch @4 + 20-B entries (Java .class shares `cafebabe`; small nfat_arch = fat). Emit hex in the same `0x%0Nx` width as the field's `uNN` |\n67\t| exe-extension decoy (`.exe` that is text/zip/PNG, `MZ` with no/garbled `PE\\0\\0` at e_lfanew) | header absent -> literal `none` if the syntax offers it; never fall back to a later `PE\\0\\0` hit or the extension |\n68\t| \"impostor\", \"renamed\", \"disguise\" | trust magic bytes at offset 0; a matching string deeper in the file is a decoy |\n69\t| answer_format syntax \"use the literal none only when the requested field is absent\" | field missing (e.g. no header) -> `none` |\n70\t| answer_format kind `json` | `json.dumps(v, separators=(\",\",\":\"), ensure_ascii=False)` -- compact, no spaces, no Markdown |\n71\t| Mastery `set1.`..`setN.` ids, artifact `delivery N: <zip> -> <member>` or `<zip>-0N.zip -> <member>` | resolve each set's member separately; see delivery layouts below |\n72\t\n73\t## Day by day\n74\t**Day 1 — You Must Be This Hash to Ride** (identity inventory). One text member (TT `roster.csv`, Mastery a renamed\n75\t`evidence-note-copy.txt` + original). filename / size-bytes / md5 / sha1 / sha256 via `zipfile` + `hashlib`; CORRECT\n76\t~36 s first try. Mastery zip-of-zips first seen.\n77\t\n78\t**Day 2 — Looks Can Be Deceiving** (`<member>-magic-prefix-hex-16`): first 16 bytes, lowercase hex, no `0x`. CORRECT ~34 s.\n79\t- Variants: TT `readme.exe` that was UTF-8 text; Mastery set2 `disguised-report.bin` that was a PDF.\n80\t- TT question text named `roster.csv` while `answer_ids` said `readme-executable-...` and the zip held only `readme.exe`\n81\t  -> `lib.common.find_artifact_hinted` (member ~ answer-id stem). TT `expired` = pre-Homebase latency, not analysis.\n82\t- Mastery zip-of-zips broke name lookup (returned the inner zip's `PK..`) -> `find_artifact` recurses nested zips.\n83\t\n84\t**Day 3 — BOM Voyage** (`text.utf8_bom_present` enum `true`/`false`). First 3 bytes == `EF BB BF`; CORRECT ~28 s.\n85\tMastery `export-001-with-bom.txt` really had a BOM -- decide from bytes, never the name. utf16/32 variants unconfirmed.\n86\t\n87\t**Day 4 — Picture This** (`jpeg.sof_dimensions_pixels`). Walk segments by declared length to SOFn (one SOF0 @0x88) ->\n88\t`<width>x<height>` (GM-confirmed; not EXIF/filename dims). Rotation flavor not asked. CORRECT ~38 s; TT/Mastery in-window.\n89\t\n90\t**Day 5 — Chunk Norris** (`png.ihdr_dimensions_pixels`). IHDR @0x10 BE u32 width,height -> `<width>x<height>` (Day 4\n91\tform by analogy, accepted). IDAT/CRC/after-IEND \"passenger\" checks were diagnostics only. CORRECT ~33 s, first try.\n92\t\n93\t**Day 6 — Portable Deception** (PDF). `pdf.header_version` exact_text.\n94\t- `xxd -l 16` -> `%PDF-1.4` -> answer bare `x.y`. Only one `%PDF-` marker; no catalog `/Version`; exiftool PDFVersion agreed.\n95\t- Rules adopted (synthetic, NOT GM-judged): header must be at file start; `%PDF-` deeper (impostor) -> `none`; catalog\n96\t  `/Version` (incl. incremental updates) never changes header_version.\n97\t- Mastery: two same-named downloads addressed `delivery N: metadata-day-06-evidence.zip -> document-00N.pdf`; pre-fetched\n98\t  contract listed 003/004, live asked 006/007 -> read the live start. CORRECT ~34 s; TT in_window 2.7 s.\n99\t\n100\t**Day 7 — Seven-Zip, No Relation** (ZIP EOCD census). `zip.eocd_total_entries` integer, id `d07-zip-001-zip-eocd-total-entries`.\n101\t- Evidence zip held `evidence-drop-001.zip` (410 B, Stored, data-descriptor flag) with `room-01/item-1.txt`,\n102\t  `room-02/item-1.txt` (identical 48 B text). EOCD total-entries u16 @+10 = 2 -> answer `2` (base-10, no units).\n103\t- All variants were honest: EOCD disk/total == CD headers == LFHs, no comment/trailing bytes. The prompt's \"empty space\"\n104\t  / \"census that does not add up\" (claim vs real walk, padding, dir entries) was flavor only — not exercised, so it is\n105\t  still unknown whether the GM wants the claimed or the walked count when they differ. Answer the field = the CLAIM.\n106\t- Worker: `xxd | tail` + `7z l -slt` on triage's pre-extracted inner zip, then stdlib `struct` EOCD parser in solve.py\n107\t  (ZIP64 aware). CORRECT 57 s after start, first try. TT 3 entries (in_window 0.89 s / 7 s); Mastery set1 4, set2 5\n108\t  (1.33 s / 7 s). Pre-fetched mastery contract (003/004) matched live this time.\n109\t\n110\t**Day 8 — What's in the Box?** (`zip.central_directory_member_names`, kind `json`, id\n111\t`d07-zip-001-zip-central-directory-member-names`). Prompt: \"The count was only the beginning. Inventory every stored\n112\tpath, preserve directory context, and identify the archive whose names reveal an impossible provenance claim.\"\n113\t- Artifact: 3308 B evidence zip with 5 members (`evidence-note.txt` 33 B, `camera-001.jpg`, `panel-001.png`,\n114\t  `document-001.pdf`, and the SAME 410 B `evidence-drop-001.zip` as Day 7). Single contract = 12 fields at once.\n115\t- Key insight: the field = the inner zip's central-directory filename fields, verbatim and in CD order:\n116\t  `[\"room-01/item-1.txt\",\"room-02/item-1.txt\"]` -- the two basenames collide, so \"preserve directory context\" means keep\n117\t  the full stored path (never basename/dedupe/sort). No `../`, absolute, backslash or UTF-8/cp437 oddities appeared in\n118\t  any variant (UT extra, 2026-10-01 09:00, unix attrs); the \"impossible provenance\" decoy was NOT exercised -- still answer\n119\t  the raw CD names (the field says central_directory, not LFH, not sanitized).\n120\t- Worker: 3 tool calls -- read contract + Day 7 solver, `7z l -slt` + `xxd | tail` on the pre-extracted inner zip, then\n121\t  copied the Day 7 solve.py and added a CD walker + `json.dumps(names, separators=(\",\",\":\"), ensure_ascii=False)`.\n122\t  Start 15:43:55Z -> CORRECT 15:44:22Z (~27 s), first try, all 12 confirmed.\n123\t- TT: 8 s window, in_window 1.15 s (solve 0.13 s), CORRECT. Mastery: 5 sets / 60 answers, 10 s window, in_window 1.34 s,\n124\t  CORRECT. Only the note's case id differed between variants.\n125\t- LIB (ratchet D8): spelling recorded as `knowledge.ZIP_CD_MEMBER_NAMES_FMT` -> `json.dumps(names, separators=(\",\",\":\"))`.\n126\t\n127\t**Day 9 — Built Different** (`pe.coff_machine_u16_hex`, kind `pattern`, syntax \"lowercase hexadecimal with a 0x prefix\",\n128\tnorm `trim`, id `d09-pe-001-pe-coff-machine-u16-hex`). Prompt: \"A software drop contains executables for several\n129\tarchitectures, plus decoys wearing executable extensions. Determine what can actually run where.\"\n130\t- Artifact: 598 KB evidence zip = the D8 kit (byte-identical apart from the case id) + `telemetry-agent-001.exe`\n131\t  (1,257,984 B, Deflate). It was an honest Go 1.22.2 PE32 console exe (buildinfo `GOOS=windows GOARCH=386`, path\n132\t  `huntress.generated/windows-pe`): e_lfanew 0x80, `PE\\0\\0`, Machine `0x014c`, 7 sections incl. `.symtab`, opt magic\n133\t  0x10b, TimeDateStamp 0. No ELF/Mach-O, no decoy exe in single, TT or any Mastery set -- the flavor was unexercised.\n134\t- Key insight: the field name is the spec -- COFF FileHeader.Machine read as a u16 and printed `0x%04x` (zero-padded to 4\n135\t  digits: `0x014c`, not `0x14c`, not `i386`). The binary lane's `machine` word (`knowledge.PE_MACHINE` -> `i386`) is a\n136\t  DIFFERENT field; don't reuse it here.\n137\t- Worker: 4 tool calls -- grep D8 solver's handlers + `jq` the pre-fetched TT/Mastery contracts (both errored: pre-start\n138\t  contracts have no `answer_ids`, harmless), `file` + `xxd -l 64` + 3-line python `struct` (0x3C -> PE sig -> u16), then\n139\t  `cp` the D8 solve.py and append a `pe-coff-machine-u16-hex` suffix branch (+ pre-armed ELF `e_machine` branch, `none`\n140\t  for MZ-without-PE decoys). Start 13:00:07.1Z -> CORRECT 13:00:54.5Z (~47 s), first try, all 13 confirmed.\n141\t- TT: 6 s window, in_window 2.88 s (submit round-trip 2.31 s, solve 0.14 s), CORRECT. Mastery: 5 sets / 65 answers, 7 s\n142\t  window, in_window 2.49 s (solve 0.86 s -- 3 MB of nested Stored zips with 1.2 MB exes), CORRECT. Only the case id (note\n143\t  hashes/magic) and exe bytes varied; Machine 0x014c everywhere.\n144\t\n145\t## GM answer conventions learned\n146\t- Filenames: exact base name incl. extension, no directory. Sizes: base-10 integer, no units. Hashes: hex, case ignored.\n147\t- Byte prefixes: lowercase hex, contiguous, exactly 2N chars (`xxd -p -l N`).\n148\t- Booleans: enum `true` / `false` (lowercase) — the contract hands the vocabulary; pick, don't probe.\n149\t- Pixel dimensions (JPEG SOF, PNG IHDR): `<width>x<height>` — width first, lowercase `x`, no spaces (GM-confirmed both,\n150\t  re-confirmed D8 `257x146` / `269x153`).\n151\t- PDF header version: bare `x.y` from the leading `%PDF-x.y` (no `PDF-`/`%` prefix); absent header -> literal `none`\n152\t  (contract wording; `none` itself not yet GM-confirmed).\n153\t- Counts (`zip.eocd_total_entries`): plain base-10 integer string, e.g. `2` (GM-confirmed D7 + D8 all modes).\n154\t- JSON lists (`zip.central_directory_member_names`): compact array, no spaces after `,`, double quotes, full stored path\n155\t  with `/` dirs, CD order -- `[\"room-01/item-1.txt\",\"room-02/item-1.txt\"]` (GM-confirmed D8 single/TT/Mastery x5).\n156\t  Whether the GM's `trim` normalization also tolerates `\", \"` spacing is untested -- always emit compact.\n157\t- Header integers as hex (`pe.coff_machine_u16_hex`): `0x` + lowercase hex zero-padded to the field width named in the\n158\t  id (`u16` -> 4 digits): `0x014c` (GM-confirmed D9 single/TT/Mastery x5). Unpadded `0x14c` untested -- don't emit it.\n159\t  Contrast: magic-prefix hex has NO `0x`; binary-lane `machine` wants the word (`i386`/`x86-64`).\n160\t- Rejected spellings: none recorded in this lane (no wrong submission in any mode, days 1-9).\n161\t- `knowledge.py`: `JPEG_DIMENSIONS_FMT`, `PNG_DIMENSIONS_FMT`, `PDF_HEADER_VERSION_FMT`, `ZIP_EOCD_TOTAL_ENTRIES_FMT`,\n162\t  `ZIP_CD_MEMBER_NAMES_FMT`, `BOOL` (PE u16-hex form not there yet -- proposed D9).\n163\t- Inference: the field id IS the spec name (`sof_dimensions_pixels` = SOF frame header, `ihdr_` = IHDR chunk,\n164\t  `header_version` = file header, `eocd_total_entries` = EOCD record's own claim, `central_directory_member_names` = CD\n165\t  file-name fields, `coff_machine_u16_hex` = COFF FileHeader.Machine as u16 hex) — read the field name literally to\n166\t  pick which structure to parse; a claimed count is NOT a CD walk / `zipfile` len, and CD names are NOT local-header\n167\t  names (they happened to agree on D7/D8). A `_uNN_hex` suffix fixes both the read width and the printed width.\n168\t\n169\t## Delivery layouts seen (resolve these before parsing)\n170\t- Single / TT: one zip; members named in `artifact` after `->` (D8: 5 members, filename question's artifact = zip only).\n171\t- Mastery days 1,2,4,5: ONE download named `...-evidence-01.zip` that is an outer zip containing `...-01.zip` and\n172\t  `...-02.zip` (zip-of-zips); each inner zip holds its set's member.\n173\t- Mastery day 7: zip-of-zips again, three levels (outer `-01.zip` holds `-01.zip` + `-02.zip`, each holding the asked\n174\t  `evidence-drop-00N.zip`); artifact ref `metadata-day-07-evidence-0N.zip -> evidence-drop-00N.zip` (no `delivery N:`).\n175\t- Mastery day 8: same shape, FIVE sets: one 17 KB download `metadata-day-08-evidence-01.zip` (Stored, UTF-8 flag) holding\n176\t  `-01.zip`..`-05.zip`, each a full 5-member kit (incl. its own `evidence-drop-001.zip`). Refs `...-evidence-0N.zip ->\n177\t  <member>`; every set reuses the same member names, so resolve by (set zip, member), never member name alone.\n178\t- Mastery day 9: same five-set shape, but the GM download is named `<challenge-id>-mastery.zip`\n179\t  (`metadata-forensics-day-09-built-different-mastery.zip`, 2.99 MB, Stored) while refs say `metadata-day-09-evidence-0N.zip\n180\t  -> <member>` -- resolve the bundle by sha256 (`lib.common.container_by_sha`), not by its filename.\n181\t- Mastery day 6: two downloads with identical filenames -> `delivery 1: <zip>` / `delivery 2: <zip>` in artifact refs.\n182\t- Member numbering shifts between pre-fetched contract and live attempt (003/004 vs 006/007) — never hardcode names.\n183\t\n184\t## Pitfalls that cost time\n185\t- Name lookup by zip filename alone breaks on zip-of-zips (returned `PK` bytes as the \"magic\") — recurse into nested zips.\n186\t- Contract question text can be stale vs `answer_ids` (Day 2 TT): answer under `answer_ids`, locate the member that exists.\n187\t- Don't let the flavor text widen the question: prompts mention impostors/passengers/orientation/provenance, but only the\n188\t  named field is graded. Answer it; keep extra checks as diagnostics.\n189\t- Container-of-containers: when the asked file is itself a zip, a naive `rfind(PK\\x05\\x06)` on the downloaded evidence\n190\t  zip reads the OUTER EOCD / CD (D8 outer CD = the 5 kit members, Mastery outer = 5 set zips). Resolve the named member's\n191\t  bytes first, then parse.\n192\t- Name-list fields: `zipfile.namelist()` is CD order but decodes non-UTF-8-flagged names as cp437 and is fine for honest\n193\t  zips; for hostile names (`../`, `/abs`, `C:\\`, `\\` separators, LFH != CD name, duplicates) emit the CD bytes as-is --\n194\t  don't let an extractor's sanitizing (7z/unzip strip `../` and leading `/`) rewrite the answer.\n195\t- Decoys by name: `*-with-bom.txt`, `.exe` that is text, `.bin` that is PDF, `.pdf` that is PNG — bytes win every time.\n196\t- Timed windows are ~5-10 s (D8: TT 8 s / Mastery 10 s; D9 shrank to 6 s / 7 s) and most of it is GM start/download/\n197\t  submit round-trips (D9 TT submit alone 2.3 s): never do anything slow (extraction to disk, exiftool, `pefile` full\n198\t  parse, subprocess) in-window; parse fixed offsets in memory. Big members (1.2 MB exe x5) pushed Mastery solve to 0.86 s\n199\t  -- decompress each member once and cache by (set zip, member).\n200\t- Executable fields: don't take `file`'s \"Intel i386\" / `pefile` machine names / the Go GOARCH token as the answer; the\n201\t  metadata field is the raw u16. And require `PE\\0\\0` exactly at e_lfanew -- an `MZ` stub alone is not a PE (decoy).\n202\t- Fastest path for a new carry-over day: copy the previous day's solver (which already answers every earlier family) and\n203\t  add only the new suffix handler -- D8 27 s, D9 47 s that way. The harness skeleton in `solver/solve.py` is NOT the\n204\t  previous day's solver; copy from `challenges/day<NN-1>/metadata-*/solver/solve.py`.\n205\t- Pre-fetched TT/Mastery `contract.json` is the HTTP 409 `start_required` body: `questions` (with ids, no sha tag) but\n206\t  NO `answer_ids` -- `jq '.answer_ids|map(..)'` errors; read `questions[].id` to preview the field set.\n207\t- Harness: re-running `hctf start` on an already-solved challenge overwrote `single_solve/start.json` and made the stop gate\n208\t  think it was incomplete (Day 2, ~2 min lost) — restore start.json from `log.jsonl`.\n209\t- Tools installed (2026-10-07): exiftool, pdfinfo/pdftotext (poppler), qpdf, mutool, pdf-parser, pdfid, pngcheck,\n210\t  zsteg, steghide, binwalk, foremost, mediainfo, sqlite3, identify/convert (ImageMagick), olevba/oleid.\n211\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"033776f4-81e5-416f-ae55-c549342e62e3","uuid":"62b9f6ef-5250-4ad6-ab2e-66b9d98e8940","timestamp":"2026-10-12T00:45:17.606Z","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/home/testpwn/huntress-2026/reference/techniques/metadata-forensics.md","content":"# metadata-forensics — technique log (days 1-9; updated after every day)\n\nHow this lane has looked so far (observations, not guarantees):\n- **Timed variants MUTATE** (organizer, Day 8: \"new, dynamic variations/mutations ... new unseen effects\"): nothing below is a\n  guarantee for Time Trial / Mastery -- solvers derive structure and degrade per field.\n- Every day = ONE evidence zip (`metadata-day-NN-evidence.zip`, plain Deflate, no password so far). Days 1-7: one tiny\n  member (33 B - 3 KB) and ONE structural fact. Day 8+: the zip carries the whole cumulative kit (note + jpg + png + pdf +\n  inner zip [+ D9 a 1.26 MB PE `.exe`]) and even the SINGLE contract asks every field (D8 12, D9 13 = identity + every\n  earlier day's field + the new one). The member can itself be a container (D7/8: an inner ZIP whose own EOCD / CD is\n  the asked field). Each day adds ONE member + ONE field; the previous kit members are byte-identical except the case id.\n- Day 9 crossed into EXECUTABLE headers (`pe.coff_machine_u16_hex`): the metadata lane now parses binaries too, but only\n  the raw header field -- answer the u16 as hex, not the binary lane's machine word (`i386`).\n- A new `<fmt>.<field>` family each day: identity (name/size/hashes) -> magic prefix -> `text.utf8_bom_present` ->\n  `jpeg.sof_dimensions_pixels` -> `png.ihdr_dimensions_pixels` -> `pdf.header_version` -> `zip.eocd_total_entries` ->\n  `zip.central_directory_member_names` -> `pe.coff_machine_u16_hex`. Since Day 3 the question literally names the field\n  (`Determine <fmt>.<field> for <member>`); answer ids read `dNN-<fmt>-NNN-<fmt>-<field>` (`.`/`_` -> `-`). NOTE the\n  `dNN` is the drop/member family, not the day the field appeared: Day 8's new field came as `d07-zip-001-zip-central-\n  directory-member-names`; Day 9's as `d09-pe-001-pe-coff-machine-u16-hex` (new member family -> new `dNN`).\n- The prompt's flavor text describes decoys (impostors, renamed copies, \"-with-bom\" names, EXIF/presentation lies, chunk\n  \"passengers\", catalog /Version overrides, \"impossible provenance\" names). The asked field so far was always the\n  STRUCTURAL truth from the header/record bytes; names/extensions/secondary metadata are the lie. All 9 single solves were\n  first-submit CORRECT in ~27-60 s; every TT/Mastery since Homebase (D4+) CORRECT first try.\n- The flavor promises MORE than the sample delivers (D9: \"executables for several architectures, plus decoys wearing\n  executable extensions\" -> one honest i386 PE, no ELF/Mach-O/decoy in any mode). Expect the promised cases to arrive\n  later as mutations; pre-arm the sibling parsers (ELF/Mach-O/decoy -> `none`) without guessing their spellings.\n- Titles are puns, not format hints: Day 7 \"Seven-Zip, No Relation\" was plain ZIP (PKWARE), no .7z anywhere.\n\n## Variant axes (what differs between the single, Time Trial and Mastery variants -- parse every value listed)\n- **Delivery layout** -- see \"Delivery layouts seen\" below; resolve the named member through whatever wrapper arrives.\n- **Decoys** -- renamed copies, misleading extensions/names, secondary metadata (EXIF, catalog /Version) that disagree\n  with the header: always answer from the structural header bytes of the member the question names.\n- **Member and values** -- names, sizes, dimensions and counts re-roll per variant; nothing about the sample is\n  constant (Day 7 entry count went 2/3/4/5 with drop number 001-004; member names `room-NN/item-K.txt`). Day 8 re-rolled\n  ONLY the note's case id (`Case <hex> evidence note.`, 33 B) -> md5/sha1/sha256/magic differ per set; jpg 257x146, png\n  269x153, pdf 1.4, eocd 2, CD names identical across single/TT/5 Mastery sets. D9 same, plus the PE: Machine 0x014c in\n  all 7 copies but the exe's sha256 differs per set (re-built per variant). Never cache a value across sets anyway.\n- **ESCALATED field set** -- the contract grows over time: D7 TT/Mastery went 1 -> 11 fields (Mastery 22); D8 started at\n  12 already in single (TT 12, Mastery 5 sets x 12 = 60); D9 13 (TT 13, Mastery 5 x 13 = 65). Families: the day's field +\n  `evidence-note-{filename,size-bytes,md5,sha1,sha256,magic-prefix-hex-16,text-utf8-bom-present}` + carry-overs\n  `d04-jpeg-*-sof-dimensions-pixels`, `d05-png-*-ihdr-dimensions-pixels`, `d06-pdf-*-header-version`, `d07-zip-*-eocd-\n  total-entries`, `d07-zip-*-central-directory-member-names`, `d09-pe-*-pe-coff-machine-u16-hex`. Dispatch on the\n  answer-id SUFFIX and keep EVERY earlier family answerable (reference: `challenges/day09/metadata-built-different/\n  solver/solve.py` answers all 13 + a pre-armed `elf-e-machine-u16-hex` branch).\n- **Answer kinds** -- `exact_text`, `integer`, `pattern` (hashes, case-insensitive; D9 also `0x`-hex with `trim` only,\n  so case MATTERS -> lowercase), `enum` (`accepted_values`), and since D8 `json` (\"compact valid JSON array with exact\n  values and order\"). Emit per `answer_format.kind`; read `syntax` for prefix/case (`0x` yes for u16_hex, no for magic).\n- **Question-text tags** (D9 TT/Mastery, new): the first question gets ` [assigned-artifact-sha256:<64 hex>]` appended\n  (Mastery: the bundle's sha, same for every set). Strip `\\s*\\[[^\\]]*\\]$` before reading a member name from question\n  text; route by `answer_id` + `artifact` instead (the D9 solver was unaffected for that reason).\n- **Nesting depth** -- the asked file may sit 2-3 zips deep (Mastery D7: outer -> `...-evidence-0N.zip` ->\n  `evidence-drop-00N.zip`); resolve by the name after `->`, never answer from an enclosing zip.\n\n## Recognition cues -> first move\n| You see | First move |\n|---|---|\n| `<zip> -> <member>` in `questions[].artifact` | `7z l -slt <zip>` then `7z x -o work/ <zip>`; (or python `zipfile` read of the member) |\n| filename / size / md5 / sha1 / sha256 | `stat -c %s`, `md5sum sha1sum sha256sum` on the extracted member (bytes, not the zip entry name) |\n| \"first sixteen bytes\", \"magic\", \"extension claims\" | `xxd -p -l 16 <member>` (lowercase, no spaces); `file -k` only for orientation |\n| `text.*_bom_present` | `xxd -l 4`: UTF-8 BOM = `ef bb bf` (UTF-16LE `ff fe`, BE `fe ff`, UTF-32LE `ff fe 00 00`) -> `true`/`false` |\n| `jpeg.*dimensions*` / SOF | walk JPEG segments from `ffd8` by length to SOFn (`ffc0..ffcf` minus c4/c8/cc): P, Y=height, X=width. `exiftool -ImageSize` cross-check only |\n| `png.ihdr_*` / \"walk their chunks\" | `xxd -s 16 -l 8` = IHDR width,height (BE u32). Chunk walk = len/type/data/CRC loop (`lib.stego.png_chunks`) |\n| `zip.eocd_*` / \"count what the archives claim\" | of the NAMED inner zip (not the evidence zip): last `PK\\x05\\x06` whose comment len reaches EOF; u16 @+8 disk entries, @+10 total, u32 @+12 cd size, @+16 cd offset, u16 @+20 comment len. `0xFFFF` -> ZIP64 locator `PK\\x06\\x07` (EOCD-20) -> `PK\\x06\\x06` u64 @+32. Cross-check: count `PK\\x01\\x02` walking from cd offset, `PK\\x03\\x04` |\n| `zip.central_directory_*` / \"inventory every stored path, preserve directory context\" | walk `PK\\x01\\x02` from EOCD cd-offset (fallback `EOCD - cd_size` if data prepended): name len u16 @+28, extra @+30, comment @+32, name at +46; next = +46+n+e+c. Raw stored path, CD order, no basename/dedupe/sort; decode UTF-8 (flag bit 11 `0x800`, else try UTF-8 then cp437). `7z l -slt` / `zipinfo -1` as cross-check |\n| `pdf.header_version` / \"declared versions\" | `head -c 16 <f> | xxd` -> `%PDF-x.y` at offset 0; `grep -a -o '/Version[^/>]*'` only as a diagnostic |\n| `pe.coff_*` / \"executables for several architectures\", `.exe`/`.dll`/`.sys` | `MZ`@0 -> e_lfanew u32 LE @0x3C -> require `PE\\0\\0` there -> COFF FileHeader: Machine u16 @+4, NumberOfSections @+6, TimeDateStamp @+8, SizeOfOptionalHeader @+20, Characteristics @+22; OptionalHeader magic @+24 (`0x10b` PE32 / `0x20b` PE32+). `xxd -s $((0x3c)) -l 4` then `xxd -s <lfanew> -l 8`. `file`/`pefile` cross-check only |\n| `elf.*` / `macho.*` siblings (promised \"several architectures\", not yet asked) | ELF: `\\x7fELF`, EI_DATA @5 picks endianness, e_machine u16 @18. Mach-O: `feedface`/`feedfacf` (either byte order) cputype u32 @4; fat `cafebabe` = BE nfat_arch @4 + 20-B entries (Java .class shares `cafebabe`; small nfat_arch = fat). Emit hex in the same `0x%0Nx` width as the field's `uNN` |\n| exe-extension decoy (`.exe` that is text/zip/PNG, `MZ` with no/garbled `PE\\0\\0` at e_lfanew) | header absent -> literal `none` if the syntax offers it; never fall back to a later `PE\\0\\0` hit or the extension |\n| \"impostor\", \"renamed\", \"disguise\" | trust magic bytes at offset 0; a matching string deeper in the file is a decoy |\n| answer_format syntax \"use the literal none only when the requested field is absent\" | field missing (e.g. no header) -> `none` |\n| answer_format kind `json` | `json.dumps(v, separators=(\",\",\":\"), ensure_ascii=False)` -- compact, no spaces, no Markdown |\n| Mastery `set1.`..`setN.` ids, artifact `delivery N: <zip> -> <member>` or `<zip>-0N.zip -> <member>` | resolve each set's member separately; see delivery layouts below |\n\n## Day by day\n**Day 1 — You Must Be This Hash to Ride** (identity inventory). One text member (TT `roster.csv`, Mastery a renamed\n`evidence-note-copy.txt` + original). filename / size-bytes / md5 / sha1 / sha256 via `zipfile` + `hashlib`; CORRECT\n~36 s first try. Mastery zip-of-zips first seen.\n\n**Day 2 — Looks Can Be Deceiving** (`<member>-magic-prefix-hex-16`): first 16 bytes, lowercase hex, no `0x`. CORRECT ~34 s.\n- Variants: TT `readme.exe` that was UTF-8 text; Mastery set2 `disguised-report.bin` that was a PDF.\n- TT question text named `roster.csv` while `answer_ids` said `readme-executable-...` and the zip held only `readme.exe`\n  -> `lib.common.find_artifact_hinted` (member ~ answer-id stem). TT `expired` = pre-Homebase latency, not analysis.\n- Mastery zip-of-zips broke name lookup (returned the inner zip's `PK..`) -> `find_artifact` recurses nested zips.\n\n**Day 3 — BOM Voyage** (`text.utf8_bom_present` enum `true`/`false`). First 3 bytes == `EF BB BF`; CORRECT ~28 s.\nMastery `export-001-with-bom.txt` really had a BOM -- decide from bytes, never the name. utf16/32 variants unconfirmed.\n\n**Day 4 — Picture This** (`jpeg.sof_dimensions_pixels`). Walk segments by declared length to SOFn (one SOF0 @0x88) ->\n`<width>x<height>` (GM-confirmed; not EXIF/filename dims). Rotation flavor not asked. CORRECT ~38 s; TT/Mastery in-window.\n\n**Day 5 — Chunk Norris** (`png.ihdr_dimensions_pixels`). IHDR @0x10 BE u32 width,height -> `<width>x<height>` (Day 4\nform by analogy, accepted). IDAT/CRC/after-IEND \"passenger\" checks were diagnostics only. CORRECT ~33 s, first try.\n\n**Day 6 — Portable Deception** (PDF). `pdf.header_version` exact_text.\n- `xxd -l 16` -> `%PDF-1.4` -> answer bare `x.y`. Only one `%PDF-` marker; no catalog `/Version`; exiftool PDFVersion agreed.\n- Rules adopted (synthetic, NOT GM-judged): header must be at file start; `%PDF-` deeper (impostor) -> `none`; catalog\n  `/Version` (incl. incremental updates) never changes header_version.\n- Mastery: two same-named downloads addressed `delivery N: metadata-day-06-evidence.zip -> document-00N.pdf`; pre-fetched\n  contract listed 003/004, live asked 006/007 -> read the live start. CORRECT ~34 s; TT in_window 2.7 s.\n\n**Day 7 — Seven-Zip, No Relation** (ZIP EOCD census). `zip.eocd_total_entries` integer, id `d07-zip-001-zip-eocd-total-entries`.\n- Evidence zip held `evidence-drop-001.zip` (410 B, Stored, data-descriptor flag) with `room-01/item-1.txt`,\n  `room-02/item-1.txt` (identical 48 B text). EOCD total-entries u16 @+10 = 2 -> answer `2` (base-10, no units).\n- All variants were honest: EOCD disk/total == CD headers == LFHs, no comment/trailing bytes. The prompt's \"empty space\"\n  / \"census that does not add up\" (claim vs real walk, padding, dir entries) was flavor only — not exercised, so it is\n  still unknown whether the GM wants the claimed or the walked count when they differ. Answer the field = the CLAIM.\n- Worker: `xxd | tail` + `7z l -slt` on triage's pre-extracted inner zip, then stdlib `struct` EOCD parser in solve.py\n  (ZIP64 aware). CORRECT 57 s after start, first try. TT 3 entries (in_window 0.89 s / 7 s); Mastery set1 4, set2 5\n  (1.33 s / 7 s). Pre-fetched mastery contract (003/004) matched live this time.\n\n**Day 8 — What's in the Box?** (`zip.central_directory_member_names`, kind `json`, id\n`d07-zip-001-zip-central-directory-member-names`). Prompt: \"The count was only the beginning. Inventory every stored\npath, preserve directory context, and identify the archive whose names reveal an impossible provenance claim.\"\n- Artifact: 3308 B evidence zip with 5 members (`evidence-note.txt` 33 B, `camera-001.jpg`, `panel-001.png`,\n  `document-001.pdf`, and the SAME 410 B `evidence-drop-001.zip` as Day 7). Single contract = 12 fields at once.\n- Key insight: the field = the inner zip's central-directory filename fields, verbatim and in CD order:\n  `[\"room-01/item-1.txt\",\"room-02/item-1.txt\"]` -- the two basenames collide, so \"preserve directory context\" means keep\n  the full stored path (never basename/dedupe/sort). No `../`, absolute, backslash or UTF-8/cp437 oddities appeared in\n  any variant (UT extra, 2026-10-01 09:00, unix attrs); the \"impossible provenance\" decoy was NOT exercised -- still answer\n  the raw CD names (the field says central_directory, not LFH, not sanitized).\n- Worker: 3 tool calls -- read contract + Day 7 solver, `7z l -slt` + `xxd | tail` on the pre-extracted inner zip, then\n  copied the Day 7 solve.py and added a CD walker + `json.dumps(names, separators=(\",\",\":\"), ensure_ascii=False)`.\n  Start 15:43:55Z -> CORRECT 15:44:22Z (~27 s), first try, all 12 confirmed.\n- TT: 8 s window, in_window 1.15 s (solve 0.13 s), CORRECT. Mastery: 5 sets / 60 answers, 10 s window, in_window 1.34 s,\n  CORRECT. Only the note's case id differed between variants.\n- LIB (ratchet D8): spelling recorded as `knowledge.ZIP_CD_MEMBER_NAMES_FMT` -> `json.dumps(names, separators=(\",\",\":\"))`.\n\n**Day 9 — Built Different** (`pe.coff_machine_u16_hex`, kind `pattern`, syntax \"lowercase hexadecimal with a 0x prefix\",\nnorm `trim`, id `d09-pe-001-pe-coff-machine-u16-hex`). Prompt: \"A software drop contains executables for several\narchitectures, plus decoys wearing executable extensions. Determine what can actually run where.\"\n- Artifact: 598 KB evidence zip = the D8 kit (byte-identical apart from the case id) + `telemetry-agent-001.exe`\n  (1,257,984 B, Deflate). It was an honest Go 1.22.2 PE32 console exe (buildinfo `GOOS=windows GOARCH=386`, path\n  `huntress.generated/windows-pe`): e_lfanew 0x80, `PE\\0\\0`, Machine `0x014c`, 7 sections incl. `.symtab`, opt magic\n  0x10b, TimeDateStamp 0. No ELF/Mach-O, no decoy exe in single, TT or any Mastery set -- the flavor was unexercised.\n- Key insight: the field name is the spec -- COFF FileHeader.Machine read as a u16 and printed `0x%04x` (zero-padded to 4\n  digits: `0x014c`, not `0x14c`, not `i386`). The binary lane's `machine` word (`knowledge.PE_MACHINE` -> `i386`) is a\n  DIFFERENT field; don't reuse it here.\n- Worker: 4 tool calls -- grep D8 solver's handlers + `jq` the pre-fetched TT/Mastery contracts (both errored: pre-start\n  contracts have no `answer_ids`, harmless), `file` + `xxd -l 64` + 3-line python `struct` (0x3C -> PE sig -> u16), then\n  `cp` the D8 solve.py and append a `pe-coff-machine-u16-hex` suffix branch (+ pre-armed ELF `e_machine` branch, `none`\n  for MZ-without-PE decoys). Start 13:00:07.1Z -> CORRECT 13:00:54.5Z (~47 s), first try, all 13 confirmed.\n- TT: 6 s window, in_window 2.88 s (submit round-trip 2.31 s, solve 0.14 s), CORRECT. Mastery: 5 sets / 65 answers, 7 s\n  window, in_window 2.49 s (solve 0.86 s -- 3 MB of nested Stored zips with 1.2 MB exes), CORRECT. Only the case id (note\n  hashes/magic) and exe bytes varied; Machine 0x014c everywhere.\n\n## GM answer conventions learned\n- Filenames: exact base name incl. extension, no directory. Sizes: base-10 integer, no units. Hashes: hex, case ignored.\n- Byte prefixes: lowercase hex, contiguous, exactly 2N chars (`xxd -p -l N`).\n- Booleans: enum `true` / `false` (lowercase) — the contract hands the vocabulary; pick, don't probe.\n- Pixel dimensions (JPEG SOF, PNG IHDR): `<width>x<height>` — width first, lowercase `x`, no spaces (GM-confirmed both,\n  re-confirmed D8 `257x146` / `269x153`).\n- PDF header version: bare `x.y` from the leading `%PDF-x.y` (no `PDF-`/`%` prefix); absent header -> literal `none`\n  (contract wording; `none` itself not yet GM-confirmed).\n- Counts (`zip.eocd_total_entries`): plain base-10 integer string, e.g. `2` (GM-confirmed D7 + D8 all modes).\n- JSON lists (`zip.central_directory_member_names`): compact array, no spaces after `,`, double quotes, full stored path\n  with `/` dirs, CD order -- `[\"room-01/item-1.txt\",\"room-02/item-1.txt\"]` (GM-confirmed D8 single/TT/Mastery x5).\n  Whether the GM's `trim` normalization also tolerates `\", \"` spacing is untested -- always emit compact.\n- Header integers as hex (`pe.coff_machine_u16_hex`): `0x` + lowercase hex zero-padded to the field width named in the\n  id (`u16` -> 4 digits): `0x014c` (GM-confirmed D9 single/TT/Mastery x5). Unpadded `0x14c` untested -- don't emit it.\n  Contrast: magic-prefix hex has NO `0x`; binary-lane `machine` wants the word (`i386`/`x86-64`).\n- Rejected spellings: none recorded in this lane (no wrong submission in any mode, days 1-9).\n- `knowledge.py`: `JPEG_DIMENSIONS_FMT`, `PNG_DIMENSIONS_FMT`, `PDF_HEADER_VERSION_FMT`, `ZIP_EOCD_TOTAL_ENTRIES_FMT`,\n  `ZIP_CD_MEMBER_NAMES_FMT`, `BOOL` (PE u16-hex form not there yet -- proposed D9).\n- Inference: the field id IS the spec name (`sof_dimensions_pixels` = SOF frame header, `ihdr_` = IHDR chunk,\n  `header_version` = file header, `eocd_total_entries` = EOCD record's own claim, `central_directory_member_names` = CD\n  file-name fields, `coff_machine_u16_hex` = COFF FileHeader.Machine as u16 hex) — read the field name literally to\n  pick which structure to parse; a claimed count is NOT a CD walk / `zipfile` len, and CD names are NOT local-header\n  names (they happened to agree on D7/D8). A `_uNN_hex` suffix fixes both the read width and the printed width.\n\n## Delivery layouts seen (resolve these before parsing)\n- Single / TT: one zip; members named in `artifact` after `->` (D8: 5 members, filename question's artifact = zip only).\n- Mastery days 1,2,4,5: ONE download named `...-evidence-01.zip` that is an outer zip containing `...-01.zip` and\n  `...-02.zip` (zip-of-zips); each inner zip holds its set's member.\n- Mastery day 7: zip-of-zips again, three levels (outer `-01.zip` holds `-01.zip` + `-02.zip`, each holding the asked\n  `evidence-drop-00N.zip`); artifact ref `metadata-day-07-evidence-0N.zip -> evidence-drop-00N.zip` (no `delivery N:`).\n- Mastery day 8: same shape, FIVE sets: one 17 KB download `metadata-day-08-evidence-01.zip` (Stored, UTF-8 flag) holding\n  `-01.zip`..`-05.zip`, each a full 5-member kit (incl. its own `evidence-drop-001.zip`). Refs `...-evidence-0N.zip ->\n  <member>`; every set reuses the same member names, so resolve by (set zip, member), never member name alone.\n- Mastery day 9: same five-set shape, but the GM download is named `<challenge-id>-mastery.zip`\n  (`metadata-forensics-day-09-built-different-mastery.zip`, 2.99 MB, Stored) while refs say `metadata-day-09-evidence-0N.zip\n  -> <member>` -- resolve the bundle by sha256 (`lib.common.container_by_sha`), not by its filename.\n- Mastery day 6: two downloads with identical filenames -> `delivery 1: <zip>` / `delivery 2: <zip>` in artifact refs.\n- Member numbering shifts between pre-fetched contract and live attempt (003/004 vs 006/007) — never hardcode names.\n\n## Pitfalls that cost time\n- Name lookup by zip filename alone breaks on zip-of-zips (returned `PK` bytes as the \"magic\") — recurse into nested zips.\n- Contract question text can be stale vs `answer_ids` (Day 2 TT): answer under `answer_ids`, locate the member that exists.\n- Don't let the flavor text widen the question: prompts mention impostors/passengers/orientation/provenance, but only the\n  named field is graded. Answer it; keep extra checks as diagnostics.\n- Container-of-containers: when the asked file is itself a zip, a naive `rfind(PK\\x05\\x06)` on the downloaded evidence\n  zip reads the OUTER EOCD / CD (D8 outer CD = the 5 kit members, Mastery outer = 5 set zips). Resolve the named member's\n  bytes first, then parse.\n- Name-list fields: `zipfile.namelist()` is CD order but decodes non-UTF-8-flagged names as cp437 and is fine for honest\n  zips; for hostile names (`../`, `/abs`, `C:\\`, `\\` separators, LFH != CD name, duplicates) emit the CD bytes as-is --\n  don't let an extractor's sanitizing (7z/unzip strip `../` and leading `/`) rewrite the answer.\n- Decoys by name: `*-with-bom.txt`, `.exe` that is text, `.bin` that is PDF, `.pdf` that is PNG — bytes win every time.\n- Timed windows are ~5-10 s (D8: TT 8 s / Mastery 10 s; D9 shrank to 6 s / 7 s) and most of it is GM start/download/\n  submit round-trips (D9 TT submit alone 2.3 s): never do anything slow (extraction to disk, exiftool, `pefile` full\n  parse, subprocess) in-window; parse fixed offsets in memory. Big members (1.2 MB exe x5) pushed Mastery solve to 0.86 s\n  -- decompress each member once and cache by (set zip, member).\n- Executable fields: don't take `file`'s \"Intel i386\" / `pefile` machine names / the Go GOARCH token as the answer; the\n  metadata field is the raw u16. And require `PE\\0\\0` exactly at e_lfanew -- an `MZ` stub alone is not a PE (decoy).\n- Fastest path for a new carry-over day: copy the previous day's solver (which already answers every earlier family) and\n  add only the new suffix handler -- D8 27 s, D9 47 s that way. The harness skeleton in `solver/solve.py` is NOT the\n  previous day's solver; copy from `challenges/day<NN-1>/metadata-*/solver/solve.py`.\n- Pre-fetched TT/Mastery `contract.json` is the HTTP 409 `start_required` body: `questions` (with ids, no sha tag) but\n  NO `answer_ids` -- `jq '.answer_ids|map(..)'` errors; read `questions[].id` to preview the field set.\n- Harness: re-running `hctf start` on an already-solved challenge overwrote `single_solve/start.json` and made the stop gate\n  think it was incomplete (Day 2, ~2 min lost) — restore start.json from `log.jsonl`.\n- Tools installed (2026-10-07): exiftool, pdfinfo/pdftotext (poppler), qpdf, mutool, pdf-parser, pdfid, pngcheck,\n  zsteg, steghide, binwalk, foremost, mediainfo, sqlite3, identify/convert (ImageMagick), olevba/oleid.\n","numLines":211,"startLine":1,"totalLines":211}},"tool_result_meta":[{"id":"toolu_01SMVv1yAkhdxn245jCp7Sji","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}]}
