{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CfwRFKxn8gBudcDpimCj3","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01284x2tosPM7WFgRgZ9bbes","name":"Bash","input":{"command":"cd /home/testpwn/huntress-2026 && python3 - <<'EOF'\np='reference/techniques/metadata-forensics.md'; s=open(p).read()\ndef rep(old,new):\n    global s\n    assert s.count(old)==1, old[:60]; s=s.replace(old,new)\nrep(\"(days 1-9; updated after every day)\",\"(days 1-10; updated after every day)\")\nrep(\"\"\"- Day 9 crossed into EXECUTABLE headers (`pe.coff_machine_u16_hex`): the metadata lane now parses binaries too, but only\n  the raw header field -- answer the u16 as hex, not the binary lane's machine word (`i386`).\"\"\",\n\"\"\"- Day 9 crossed into EXECUTABLE headers (`pe.coff_machine_u16_hex`): the metadata lane now parses binaries too, but only\n  the raw header field -- answer the u16 as hex, not the binary lane's machine word (`i386`). Day 10 stayed on the SAME\n  PE (`pe.address_of_entry_point_rva_hex`) and DE-escalated: zip = the exe only, contract = 1 field (TT 1, Mastery 2x1).\"\"\")\nrep(\"\"\"`zip.central_directory_member_names` -> `pe.coff_machine_u16_hex`. Since Day 3\"\"\",\"\"\"`zip.central_directory_member_names` -> `pe.coff_machine_u16_hex` -> `pe.address_of_entry_point_rva_hex`. Since Day 3\"\"\")\nrep(\"\"\"Day 9's as `d09-pe-001-pe-coff-machine-u16-hex` (new member family -> new `dNN`).\"\"\",\"\"\"Day 9's as `d09-pe-001-pe-coff-machine-u16-hex` (new member family -> new `dNN`); Day 10's as `d09-pe-001-pe-address-of-entry-point-rva-hex` (same exe family).\"\"\")\nrep(\"\"\"STRUCTURAL truth from the header/record bytes; names/extensions/secondary metadata are the lie. All 9 single solves were\n  first-submit CORRECT in ~27-60 s; every TT/Mastery since Homebase (D4+) CORRECT first try.\"\"\",\"\"\"STRUCTURAL truth from the header/record bytes; names/extensions/secondary metadata are the lie. Singles D1-D9 were\n  first-submit CORRECT in ~27-60 s; D10 took one wrong spelling (unpadded hex). Every TT/Mastery since D4 CORRECT first try.\"\"\")\nrep(\"\"\"all 7 copies but the exe's sha256 differs per set (re-built per variant). Never cache a value across sets anyway.\"\"\",\"\"\"all 7 copies but the exe's sha256 differs per set (re-built per variant). D10: the entry RVA re-rolled per variant\n  (single 0x00065bd0, TT 0x00063a80, Mastery 0x00063510 / 0x00065bd0). Never cache a value across sets.\"\"\")\nrep(\"\"\"- **ESCALATED field set** -- the contract grows over time: D7 TT/Mastery went 1 -> 11 fields (Mastery 22); D8 started at\n  12 already in single (TT 12, Mastery 5 sets x 12 = 60); D9 13 (TT 13, Mastery 5 x 13 = 65).\"\"\",\"\"\"- **Field-set size** -- grows AND shrinks: D7 TT/Mastery went 1 -> 11 fields (Mastery 22); D8 12 in every mode (Mastery\n  5 x 12); D9 13 (Mastery 5 x 13); D10 back to ONE field everywhere (Mastery 2 sets x 1, zip = the lone exe).\"\"\")\nrep(\"\"\"  solver/solve.py` answers all 13 + a pre-armed `elf-e-machine-u16-hex` branch).\"\"\",\"\"\"  solver/solve.py` answers all 13; `day10/metadata-where-do-we-begin/solver/solve.py` = those + entry/image-base/opt-magic\n  /ELF e_entry branches).\"\"\")\nrep(\"\"\"| `pe.coff_*` / \"executables for several architectures\", `.exe`/`.dll`/`.sys` | `MZ`@0 -> e_lfanew u32 LE @0x3C -> require `PE\\\\0\\\\0` there -> COFF FileHeader: Machine u16 @+4, NumberOfSections @+6, TimeDateStamp @+8, SizeOfOptionalHeader @+20, Characteristics @+22; OptionalHeader magic @+24 (`0x10b` PE32 / `0x20b` PE32+). `xxd -s $((0x3c)) -l 4` then `xxd -s <lfanew> -l 8`. `file`/`pefile` cross-check only |\"\"\",\n\"\"\"| `pe.coff_*` / \"executables for several architectures\", `.exe`/`.dll`/`.sys` | `MZ`@0 -> e_lfanew u32 LE @0x3C -> require `PE\\\\0\\\\0` there -> COFF FileHeader: Machine u16 @+4, NumberOfSections @+6, TimeDateStamp @+8, SizeOfOptionalHeader @+20, Characteristics @+22; OptionalHeader magic @+24 (`0x10b` PE32 / `0x20b` PE32+