","+a 0x prefix\", norm `trim`, id `d09-pe-001-pe-address-of-entry-point-rva-hex`). Prompt: \"Architecture tells you whether a","+binary can run; its entry point tells you where execution begins. Map the start addresses and catch the report that is","+lying.\"","+- Artifact: 595 KB zip holding ONLY `telemetry-agent-001.exe` (the D9 Go 1.22 386 PE32, 1,257,984 B, ImageBase 0x400000).","+  The D8 kit and every carry-over field were gone: 1 field in single, 1 in TT, 2 sets x 1 in Mastery. No \"report\" or","+  second binary anywhere -- the \"lying report\" flavor was unexercised.","+- Key insight: OptionalHeader.AddressOfEntryPoint (u32 @ e_lfanew+24+16) = 0x65bd0, printed `0x%08x` -> `0x00065bd0`.","+  Unpadded `0x65bd0` was REJECTED (first wrong submit in this lane): a `_hex` header field is zero-padded to its struct","+  width even when the id has no `uNN` (D9 u16 -> 4 digits, D10 u32 -> 8). objdump's `start address 0x00465bd0` is the","+  VA (ImageBase + RVA) -- not the asked RVA.","+- Worker: the harness skeleton (not the D9 solver) was in solver/, so it spliced D9's handlers in by `sed` (~30 s), then","+  `od -tx4 -j$((lfanew+40))`. Start 00:41:26Z -> incorrect 00:42:24 -> CORRECT 00:42:41 (~75 s, 1 wrong). Solver also","+  pre-arms image_base (PE32 `0x%08x`, PE32+ `0x%016x`), opt magic `0x%04x`, ELF e_entry (`0x%08x`/`0x%016x`) -- those","+  widths are the same rule by analogy, NOT GM-confirmed.","+- TT 8 s window, in_window 0.79 s (solve 0.03 s); Mastery 11 s, 0.77 s. Both CORRECT; RVA differed per variant."," "," ## GM answer conventions learned"," - Filenames: exact base name incl. extension, no directory. Sizes: base-10 integer, no units. Hashes: hex, case ignored."]},{"oldStart":154,"oldLines":12,"newStart":159,"newLines":14,"lines":[" - JSON lists (`zip.central_directory_member_names`): compact array, no spaces after `,`, double quotes, full stored path","   with `/` dirs, CD order -- `[\"room-01/item-1.txt\",\"room-02/item-1.txt\"]` (GM-confirmed D8 single/TT/Mastery x5).","   Whether the GM's `trim` normalization also tolerates `\", \"` spacing is untested -- always emit compact.","-- Header integers as hex (`pe.coff_machine_u16_hex`): `0x` + lowercase hex zero-padded to the field width named in the","-  id (`u16` -> 4 digits): `0x014c` (GM-confirmed D9 single/TT/Mastery x5). Unpadded `0x14c` untested -- don't emit it.","-  Contrast: magic-prefix hex has NO `0x`; binary-lane `machine` wants the word (`i386`/`x86-64`).","-- Rejected spellings: none recorded in this lane (no wrong submission in any mode, days 1-9).","+- Header integers as hex (`*_hex`): `0x` + lowercase hex ZERO-PADDED to the struct field's width: u16 Machine ->","+  `0x014c` (D9), u32 AddressOfEntryPoint -> `0x00065bd0` (D10, all modes). The width comes from the STRUCT, not the id","+  (D10's id has no `u32`). Contrast: magic-prefix hex has NO `0x`; binary-lane `machine` wants the word (`i386`), and the","+  binary lane's `entry_point` was accepted UNPADDED (`0x401040`) -- different lane, different generator.","+- Rejected spellings: `0x65bd0` for pe.address_of_entry_point_rva_hex (D10 single; unpadded) -- the only one, days 1-10."," - `knowledge.py`: `JPEG_DIMENSIONS_FMT`, `PNG_DIMENSIONS_FMT`, `PDF_HEADER_VERSION_FMT`, `ZIP_EOCD_TOTAL_ENTRIES_FMT`,","-  `ZIP_CD_MEMBER_NAMES_FMT`, `BOOL` (PE u16-hex form not there yet -- proposed D9).","+  `ZIP_CD_MEMBER_NAMES_FMT`, `PE_COFF_MACHINE_U16_HEX_FMT`, `PE_ENTRY_POINT_RVA_HEX_FMT` (+`_REJECTED`), `BOOL`;","+  `playbook` metadata `hex` entry carries the padding rule."," - Inference: the field id IS the spec name (`sof_dimensions_pixels` = SOF frame header, `ihdr_` = IHDR chunk,","   `header_version` = file header, `eocd_total_entries` = EOCD record's own claim, `central_directory_member_names` = CD","   file-name fields, `coff_machine_u16_hex` = COFF FileHeader.Machine as u16 hex) — read the field name literally to"]},{"oldStart":178,"oldLines":6,"newStart":185,"newLines":7,"lines":[" - Mastery day 9: same five-set shape, but the GM download is named `<challenge-id>-mastery.zip`","   (`metadata-forensics-day-09-built-different-mastery.zip`, 2.99 MB, Stored) while refs say `metadata-day-09-evidence-0N.zip","   -> <member>` -- resolve the bundle by sha256 (`lib.common.container_by_sha`), not by its filename.","+- Mastery day 10: TWO sets only, refs `metadata-day-10-evidence-0N.zip -> telemetry-agent-00N.exe` (003/004)."," - Mastery day 6: two downloads with identical filenames -> `delivery 1: <zip>` / `delivery 2: <zip>` in artifact refs."," - Member numbering shifts between pre-fetched contract and live attempt (003/004 vs 006/007) — never hardcode names."," "]},{"oldStart":199,"oldLines":9,"newStart":207,"newLines":11,"lines":["   -- decompress each member once and cache by (set zip, member)."," - Executable fields: don't take `file`'s \"Intel i386\" / `pefile` machine names / the Go GOARCH token as the answer; the","   metadata field is the raw u16. And require `PE\\0\\0` exactly at e_lfanew -- an `MZ` stub alone is not a PE (decoy).","+- Hex width (D10, cost a wrong submit + 17 s): `\"0x%x\"` drops leading zeros; print `0x%0{2*size}x` for the field's","+  struct size. RVA vs VA: `_rva` = the raw field, never ImageBase + it."," - Fastest path for a new carry-over day: copy the previous day's solver (which already answers every earlier family) and","   add only the new suffix handler -- D8 27 s, D9 47 s that way. The harness skeleton in `solver/solve.py` is NOT the","-  previous day's solver; copy from `challenges/day<NN-1>/metadata-*/solver/solve.py`.","+  previous day's solver; `cp challenges/day<NN-1>/metadata-*/solver/solve.py` over it (D10 spliced by sed instead)."," - Pre-fetched TT/Mastery `contract.json` is the HTTP 409 `start_required` body: `questions` (with ids, no sha tag) but","   NO `answer_ids` -- `jq '.answer_ids|map(..)'` errors; read `questions[].id` to preview the field set."," - Harness: re-running `hctf start` on an already-solved challenge over