g member as a PE too (format `pe`). Labels come from the header of THIS member (Go PE: format `pe`, architecture `x86-64` from Machine)."," - **Variant index per group** -- `dNN--variant-XXX` re-rolls per group and mode (D7 TT: d03-001, d04-006, d07-005 ...); sizes","   and config values change, names/layout don't. TT == Mastery set1 bytes on D7; D8 TT re-used the D7 TT old-group indices","   (d08 = variant-000); D9 TT == set1 for d02-d09 (d09 BR09-003) but d01 differed (TT variant-000 `8100`, all 5 Mastery sets one","   other d01 with `mov eax, 8104`, symtab present). Mastery d09 = BR09-003/006/001/004/007; d08 stayed variant-000..004."," - **Mastery packaging** -- `setN.` prefixed ids, each set its own `delivery N: evidence.zip` (same filename): pair by sha256.","-  Set count re-rolls: 2 (D2-D7), 5 on D8-D9 (set2/set4 had d02/d04 as PE both days): loop over every `setN.`. From D9 (all","+  Set count re-rolls: 2 (D2-D7), 5 on D8-D9 (set2/set4 had d02/d04 as PE both days), 3 on D10: loop over every `setN.`. From D9 (all","   lanes) the first question of each set ends `Evidence case: d09-m-<16hex>. [assigned-artifact-sha256:<zip sha256>]`","   (TT: `d09-tt-...`): an explicit set -> delivery map; it is question TEXT, never part of an answer."," - **answer_format.kind for the same field name** -- D8: `d01_analysis_elf_class`/`machine` exact_text (`ELF64`/`x86-64`) and","   `d08_analysis_elf_class`/`machine` integer (`64`/`62`) in ONE contract; D9 `d09_analysis_machine` integer again. Rule:","   dispatch on `kind`, not on the field name.","+- **Feature-presence fields** -- `has_<thing>_section` (D10 `has_hcfg_section`, enum true/false) for ELF AND PE: answer from the","+  member's section-name table (`.hcfg` literally; PE names are 8-byte NUL-padded), generic over `<thing>` (regex `has_(\\w+?)_section`)."," - **Field set per old group** -- old groups gain ids over days (D8 padded every group to 10). Answer by field name from the","   parsed facts dict of THAT member; an